„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections—…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ:The word of the LORD that came to Joel the son of Pethuel.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†Hear this, ye old men, and give ear, all ye inhabitants of the land. Hath this been in your days, or even in the days of your fathers?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnTell ye your children of it, and let your children tell their children, and their children another generation.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ½That which the palmerworm hath left hath the locust eaten; and that which the locust hath left hath the cankerworm eaten; and that which the cankerworm hath left hath the caterpiller eaten.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}Awake, ye drunkards, and weep; and howl, all ye drinkers of wine, because of the new wine; for it is cut off from your mouth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“For a nation is come up upon my land, strong, and without number, whose teeth are the teeth of a lion, and he hath the cheek teeth of a great lion.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†He hath laid my vine waste, and barked my fig tree: he hath made it clean bare, and cast it away; the branches thereof are made white.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHLament like a virgin girded with sackcloth for the husband of her youth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyThe meat offering and the drink offering is cut off from the house of the LORD; the priests, the LORD's ministers, mourn.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnThe field is wasted, the land mourneth; for the corn is wasted: the new wine is dried up, the oil languisheth.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙˆBe ye ashamed, O ye husbandmen; howl, O ye vinedressers, for the wheat and for the barley; because the harvest of the field is perished.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÓThe vine is dried up, and the fig tree languisheth; the pomegranate tree, the palm tree also, and the apple tree, even all the trees of the field, are withered: because joy is withered away from the sons of men.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÚGird yourselves, and lament, ye priests: howl, ye ministers of the altar: come, lie all night in sackcloth, ye ministers of my God: for the meat offering and the drink offering is withholden from the house of your God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSanctify ye a fast, call a solemn assembly, gather the elders and all the inhabitants of the land into the house of the LORD your God, and cry unto the LORD,¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkAlas for the day! for the day of the LORD is at hand, and as a destruction from the Almighty shall it come.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYIs not the meat cut off before our eyes, yea, joy and gladness from the house of our God?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyThe seed is rotten under their clods, the garners are laid desolate, the barns are broken down; for the corn is withered.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…How do the beasts groan! the herds of cattle are perplexed, because they have no pasture; yea, the flocks of sheep are made desolate.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒO LORD, to thee will I cry: for the fire hath devoured the pastures of the wilderness, and the flame hath burned all the trees of the field.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThe beasts of the field cry also unto thee: for the rivers of waters are dried up, and the fire hath devoured the pastures of the wilderness.¦layout ªlast_verse